jobs.description:
Job Summary

We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer who enjoys building scalable, high-quality applications and solving real technical challenges.

Mandatory Skill-set

Degree/Diploma in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related fields;
Must have 8+years of experience in software development;
Strong hands-on experience in C#/.NET or Java;
Experience with React/Next.js frontend (full-stack is a plus);
Production support experience preferred;
Strong problem-solving and ownership mindset;
Good understanding of testing, debugging, and code quality.

Desired Skill-set

Experience leading or mentoring AI-enhanced development teams;
Experience using AI tools for code generation, testing, or optimization.

Responsibilities

Craft effective prompts and workflows for accurate, maintainable, and secure code;
Design, evaluate, and refine AI-generated outputs against software and business requirements;
Architect scalable enterprise-grade applications using AI-assisted development practices;
Build rapid prototypes using GenAI tools and refine them toward production quality;
Integrate AI into software delivery pipelines and DevOps processes;
Perform code reviews of human-written and AI-generated code;
Maintain documentation, prompt libraries, and reusable patterns;
Collaborate with product owners, designers, and engineers;
Mentor team members on effective prompt engineering practices;
Champion ethical and responsible AI usage in engineering workflows.

Should you be interested in this career opportunity, please send in your updated resume to apply@sciente.com
at the earliest.

When you apply, you voluntarily consent to the disclosure, collection and use of your personal data for employment/recruitment and related purposes in accordance with the SCIENTE Group Privacy Policy, a copy of which is published at SCIENTE’s website (https://www.sciente.com/privacy-policy).

Confidentiality is assured, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified for interviews.
EA Licence No. 07C5639

